## Critical

### GitHub token committed to the repository — \`src/config.ts:3\`

A GitHub token is stored in the source code, so anyone with the code can use it.

- **Evidence:** \`ghp_…(40 chars)\`
- **Fix:** Revoke the token in GitHub settings, then read it from an environment variable.
- **Rule:** \`secrets/github-token\` (opscrew-secrets)
- **References:** <https://docs.github.com/en/authentication>

## High

### Table \`profiles\` has no row-level security — \`supabase/migrations/20260101000000_init.sql:3\`

Anyone with the public anon key can read and change every row.

- **Fix:** Enable row-level security and add policies | ownership checks.
- **Rule:** \`supabase/rls-disabled\` (opscrew-supabase)

## Low

### Base image uses \`latest\` — \`Dockerfile\`

A GitHub token is stored in the source code, so anyone with the code can use it.

- **Evidence:** \`FROM node:latest\`
- **Fix:** Revoke the token in GitHub settings, then read it from an environment variable.
- **Rule:** \`config/dockerfile-latest\` (opscrew-config)
- **References:** <https://docs.github.com/en/authentication>

